        "revision": 1335179728,
        "heading": "Cultivation",
        "text": "Agave polianthiflora is cultivated as an ornamental plant.  It is mostly easily propagated from seed, as it does not offset as much as other species of Agave. It prefers a shallow, well-drained soil and regular fertilization during vegetation time.\nAs a container plant grown in cold climates, during the winter it may be kept in a completely dark place.",
